# Trivy ignore file for known acceptable findings.
# Add false-positives here only after manual verification.

# golang.org/x/crypto: widely used, tracked upstream, no known exploitable CVE in our usage
golang.org/x/crypto@*

# github.com/gorilla/websocket: no exploitable CVE in our usage pattern
github.com/gorilla/websocket@*

# usr/local/bin/gosu (Dockerfile.patroni, via the postgres:16-alpine base
# image - not something we install ourselves): CVEs below are all in the Go
# stdlib gosu happens to link (crypto/tls, net/mail, net/http2, crypto/x509 -
# TLS/HTTP/mail parsing), never in code gosu exercises. gosu's own logic is
# ~50 lines: parse args, setuid/setgid, exec() the target binary - no
# networking of its own. Re-check (and prune this list) once
# postgres:16-alpine bundles a gosu built with a newer Go toolchain.
CVE-2025-68121
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2026-25679
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
